## Story Description
The get_by_supplier() endpoint in backend/app/routers/cube.py builds a SQL SELECT that includes canonical_supplier_id, canonical_supplier_name, parent_company_name, COUNT(*), SUM(base_amount), AVG(payment_terms_days) — but not abc_segment. The transactions table has an abc_segment TEXT column populated by the cube pipeline via _compute_abc_segments(). After a pipeline run, all transactions rows for a given canonical_supplier_id share the same abc_segment value. Adding MAX(abc_segment) AS abc_segment to the SELECT (compatible with the GROUP BY) will surface it in the API response. The frontend SupplierPage AbcBadge component already references row.abc_segment and renders nothing when it is undefined.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: backend/app/routers/cube.py — in get_by_supplier(), change the data_sql f-string SELECT clause to include MAX(abc_segment) AS abc_segment after AVG(payment_terms_days). The full SELECT list should be: canonical_supplier_id, canonical_supplier_name, parent_company_name, COUNT(*) AS transaction_count, SUM(base_amount) AS total_spend, AVG(payment_terms_days) AS avg_payment_days, MAX(abc_segment) AS abc_segment
- Edit file: backend/app/routers/cube.py — in the list comprehension that builds the data list (the block starting 'data = [' after the conn.execute calls), add 'abc_segment': (r['abc_segment'] if r['abc_segment'] is not None else None) to each row dict
- Run: cd backend && python -m pytest tests/test_cube_api.py -v — all existing tests must pass
- Verify: the keys of each dict in the 'data' list returned by get_by_supplier() now include 'abc_segment'

